`UNUSED_CONSTANT` with the comment "Unused import that should be caught by linting" is a test artifact. It is not an import and the comment is misleading. It will fail lint's no-unused-vars rule or ship as dead code.

::diff{file="packages/features/feature-opt-in/config.ts" lines="4-5"}

Remove both lines.

Replacing the single `HAS_OPT_IN_FEATURES` gate with `HAS_USER_OPT_IN_FEATURES`, `HAS_TEAM_OPT_IN_FEATURES`, and `HAS_ORG_OPT_IN_FEATURES` in `SettingsLayoutAppDirClient.tsx` is the right shape. The user, org, and team tabs now each appear only when some feature is available at that level.

::diff{file="apps/web/app/(use-page-wrapper)/settings/(settings-layout)/SettingsLayoutAppDirClient.tsx" lines="78-86"}

The flags are computed once at module load from the static `OPT_IN_FEATURES`, which is fine since that list is static config. The defaults-to-all-scopes rule (`!f.scope || f.scope.includes(...)`) is applied consistently across the flags, the filter helper, and the validator. That consistency is worth keeping.
